A healthcare team added a hook to `.claude/settings.json` to block destructive shell commands:

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      { "matcher": "bash",
        "hooks": [ { "type": "command", "command": "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/block-rm.sh" } ] }
    ]
  }
}
```

The script prints a denial message and exits with code 1 when it sees `rm -rf`. `/hooks` lists the hook under PreToolUse, but a `claude --debug` session shows the PreToolUse event evaluated for `rm -rf build/` with no matcher match and the command running. Which change fixes the reported problem?
